A||||5||Greg Piet||3.1 Stroker redline||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||05-13-2001||06:54 PM||||What would be a conservative yet not ridiculously low red line for the typical 2.8 to 3.1 stroker upgrade?<P>If I am not mistaken increasing the stroke reduces the "safe" red line for a given motor.<P>I was planning on 5500-5700 RPM for my rev limiter, but is that too high?||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||05-13-2001||09:07 PM||||If you use ARP rod bolts and main studs than 6000 rpm would be not a problem. With the proper camshaft and valve train 6500 rpm would be safe too. Get the Chevy power book and follow the recommendations for improving the oiling system and you should be good to go. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||05-14-2001||12:47 PM||||One other thing to consider, since the 3.1 is basically a stroked 2.8 anyway, you should be fine with the factory redline on a 3.1.  Now, if someone with a 3.1 would kindly post the redline on it, you'll have a good starting figure.  I'm guessing 6000 would be max.  You should be plenty safe with 5500-5700 rpm.  Of course, you could go higher with the proper equipment, as was mentioned. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Eric||05-14-2001||03:11 PM||||I never rev my stroker past 5700.  I'm sure it would be okay a little to the right of 6k, but the motor doesn't make power there anyway, plus you miss the ideal upshift point (atleast on my 5 speed).  A clogged cat was my problem since I rebuilt the motor.  I haven't exactly been a big advocate of the swap since for that very reason.  But now the cat is gone, and my tune has changed.  The motor is, without a doubt, stronger than the 2.8.  My gtech says low 7 seconds 0-60 with granny style easy launches (daily driver now).  Put a cam in that thing too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||05-14-2001||04:05 PM||||Hey Eric I remember you having no power from your 3.1 when you first built it. I tried to tell you it was most likely a clogged cat and gave you a vacuum test to perform. You said you did the test and it wasn't a clogged system. What happened?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||05-14-2001||06:06 PM||||Thx for the words of wisdom.<BR>From what I can gather from my camshaft spec's the peak power is from 1500 to 4000 so  I didnt think there would be anything advantageous to revving beyond 6 grand, but I wanted to be sure that 5700 wouldnt grenade on me.<P>BTW Just got the block back from the local shop...  The block should be assembled tonight!!<BR>mmmm   stroker!||||reg||1
